{# Search widget.

   Progressive enhancement, in the strict sense: this markup is inert and
   invisible until search_bar.js finds it and adds `js-search` to <html>. With
   scripting disabled it is display:none and never focusable, because the input
   is also disabled until the script enables it.

   A macro taking an `instance` name rather than a plain include, because the
   nav renders this twice — once for the desktop bar, once for the mobile
   drawer. With fixed ids both copies claimed id="site-search", which is
   invalid HTML and left the drawer's field permanently disabled: the script
   looked the element up by id and only ever found the first one.

   `data-search` is the hook the script binds to; the ids exist only for the
   ARIA wiring, which genuinely needs unique targets. #}
{% macro field(instance, settings) %}
<div class="search" role="search" data-search>
  <svg class="search-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/>
    <path d="M15.5 15.5 L21 21" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
  </svg>
  <input
    class="search-input"
    type="search"
    id="site-search-{{ instance }}"
    data-search-input
    placeholder="Search"
    autocomplete="off"
    disabled
    role="combobox"
    aria-expanded="false"
    aria-controls="search-results-{{ instance }}"
    aria-autocomplete="list"
    aria-label="Search {{ settings.name }}">
  <div class="search-results" id="search-results-{{ instance }}" data-search-results
       role="listbox" aria-label="Search results" hidden></div>
</div>
{% endmacro %}
